{"name":"Elite Blue","hex":"#1b3053","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of high birth or social position; aristocratic or patrician.","Representing the choicest or most select of a group."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A special group or social class of people who have a superior social or economic status and attendant power, advantages, or privileges in society; a member of such a group.","An individual member of such a group."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elite"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elite","blocks":[{"text":"In political and sociological theory, the elite are a small group of powerful or wealthy people who hold a disproportionate amount of wealth, privilege, political power, or skill in a group. Defined by the Cambridge Dictionary, the \"elite\" are \"the richest, most powerful, best-educated, or best-trained group in a society\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Prime_Minister_Boris_Johnson_UNGA_visit_%2851786182369%29.jpg/330px-Prime_Minister_Boris_Johnson_UNGA_visit_%2851786182369%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elite"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/500px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/1280px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg/500px-Maxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bill Clinton (left middle),[21][22] Jeffrey Epstein (right middle),[21][22][23][24] and Ghislaine Maxwell (right)[21] have been characterized as associating with the global elite.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaxwell_Epstein_Clinton_1993_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Demo-gegen-wef.jpg/500px-Demo-gegen-wef.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Demo-gegen-wef.jpg/1280px-Demo-gegen-wef.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Demo-gegen-wef.jpg/500px-Demo-gegen-wef.